# Act 3, chapter 7 "Activation" (Future Trunks's timeline, Age 767). Flags 330 chapter opened, 331 Gero killed,
# 332 outside (chapter end). Party: Seventeen = character 1 (form 14, actor 102), Eighteen = character 3 (form 23, actor 262).
# ch7_start runs straight on from the conversion scene (act2_siblings.scene) in the tank room 1:79.
list ch7_start
set_flag 330
say gero Rest while you can. Your first tests begin tomorrow.
narrate The tests did not go the way Dr. Gero planned.
narrate Seventeen ignored his orders. Eighteen laughed at them. Within a month he gave up, shut them both down and sealed them in their pods.
do call 120 60
do call 183 516 1462 1463
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1
do call 120 1; call 119 1 80 1 216 216; call 121 60
narrate Age 767. Dr. Gero's hidden laboratory.
narrate Son Goku is dead. A heart virus took him, not a fight. Gero's revenge was stolen from him.
say gero Goku is dead, and the two of you are all I have left. Wake up.
say android17 ...How long were we out?
say gero Long enough for the world to forget you. This time you will obey me, or I will shut you down for good.
say android18 That little box in your hand. That's the off switch, isn't it?
say gero Give me a reason to use it.
say android17 Here's one.
narrate Seventeen moved faster than the old man's thumb.
do call 120 30
set_flag 331
do call 119 1 81 1 216 216; call 121 60
say android18 ...That's it? He's just gone?
say android17 We're free, Eighteen. Nobody gets to tell us what to do. Not ever again.
narrate Far to the north, a machine Gero built years ago lost its creator's signal.
narrate Computer: Creator signal lost. Directive: destroy Son Goku. Target deceased. Contingency: complete Units Thirteen, Fourteen and Fifteen.
say android18 Did you hear something?
say android17 Just this place falling apart. Come on. I want to see the sky.
journal Leave Dr. Gero's hidden laboratory
do call 47; call 51 0
list eighteen_lab_talk
say android18 Don't look at me like that. I'm coming. I just wanted one more look at the pods.
# walk-in trigger at the arrival point of the Northern Wilderness 1:83 (flag 332 clear)
list ch7_end
set_flag 332
say android18 So this is outside. I'd forgotten how big it is.
say android17 Big and boring. Let's find a city and see what it's got.
say android18 Seventeen... do you remember the last city we were in?
say android17 Not really. Does it matter?
say android18 ...No. I guess it doesn't.
narrate End of Chapter 7.
run ch8_start
# ---------- the lab's lockdown (areas from log4/gen_ch7.py; flags 338 alarm, 339 Security Unit destroyed, 329 locker)
list ch7_alarm
set_flag 338
narrate Red lights. A siren, then the computer's flat voice from every speaker at once.
narrate Computer: Creator signal lost. Unregistered units in the laboratory. Lockdown. Security, purge the intruders.
say android17 Unregistered? He built us.
say android18 And now his house wants us dead. Charming.
say android17 There's a control room past this wing. We switch it off, we walk out the front door.
journal Get through the lockdown to the {c07}control room{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch7_locker
if_flag 329 locker_empty
set_flag 329
narrate Gero's workbench. Notes on Unit 16, a cold cup of tea... and a Senzu Bean in a labelled jar: "FOR EMERGENCIES".
say android18 He kept one for himself. Of course he did.
do call 129 11 1; call 129 1 1
stop
label locker_empty
narrate Gero's notes. Nothing worth reading.
list ch7_console
unless_flag 339 console_locked
narrate The security console. Seventeen finds the lockdown switch on the second try.
narrate Computer: Lockdown released. ...Continuing construction. Unit Thirteen: two percent. Fourteen: one percent. Fifteen: one percent.
say android18 More of us?
say android17 Not our problem. Let the old man's computer play with its toys.
say android18 Seventeen. If it finishes them, they'll come looking for us.
say android17 Then we'll be somewhere fun when they do. Come on.
narrate The hangar door grinds open. Cold mountain air pours in.
do call 120 30
do call 120 1; call 119 1 82 1 112 200; call 121 40
stop
label console_locked
narrate The console is behind the security machine. It isn't going to let anyone near it.
# ---------- the research archive and the bio wing (log4/gen_more.py; flags 480 archive arrival, 481 bio wing
# arrival, 482 warden destroyed, 483-485 breakers CORE / LIGHTS / DOORS (485 = power to the bio wing), 486 monitor)
list ch7_archive
set_flag 480
narrate Gero's archive. Shelves of notebooks from floor to ceiling, and terminals that never stopped running.
say android18 He wrote everything down. Everything.
say android17 Then somewhere in here it says why. Not that it matters now.
do call 47; call 51 0
list log_subjects
narrate Research log: SUBJECTS 17 AND 18.
narrate "Conversion complete. Strength beyond projections. Memory suppression: incomplete. Nothing was erased. Only buried."
narrate "I looked for the part of them that would not leave the other behind. I could not find it. It would not come out."
say android18 ...
say android17 Come on. It's just an old man's diary.
list log_units
narrate Research log: UNITS 13, 14, 15.
narrate "Designed from my own patterns. No will, no curiosity, no names. One order only: Son Goku's death."
narrate "If I fail, the computer will finish them. They will not refuse it. They are not like 17 and 18."
say android17 Not like us. He finally said something nice.
list log_cell
narrate Research log: PROJECT CELL.
narrate "The spy robot has gathered cells from every great fighter it could find. The computer will grow them into one."
narrate "It will take decades. I will not live to see it wake. My perfect creation, and I will never meet it."
say android18 Seventeen. He made something worse than us.
say android17 Then it can wait its turn.
list breaker_core
if_flag 485 brk_on
if_flag 483 brk_core_on
set_flag 483
narrate Breaker panel: CORE. The lever thunks down. Deep below, a hum starts up.
narrate Taped to the panel, in small handwriting: COLD START. CORE, LIGHTS, DOORS. IN THAT ORDER.
stop
label brk_core_on
narrate CORE is closed. The hum goes on.
stop
label brk_on
narrate All three breakers are closed. The power is on.
list breaker_lights
if_flag 485 brkl_on
if_flag 484 brkl_done
unless_flag 483 brkl_trip
set_flag 484
narrate Breaker panel: LIGHTS. The lever holds. Every light in the wing flickers, then stays on.
stop
label brkl_trip
narrate Breaker panel: LIGHTS. The lever bangs straight back up. Sparks. Nothing holds without CORE.
narrate Taped to the panel: COLD START. CORE, LIGHTS, DOORS. IN THAT ORDER.
stop
label brkl_done
narrate LIGHTS is closed.
stop
label brkl_on
narrate All three breakers are closed. The power is on.
list breaker_doors
if_flag 485 brkd_on
unless_flag 484 brkd_trip
set_flag 485
narrate Breaker panel: DOORS. The lever drops. At the bottom of the wing, the shutters over the lower corridor grind open.
say android18 The lower corridor. The sign down there said BIO WING.
do call 120 20; call 119 1 111 1 220 300; call 121 20
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label brkd_trip
do call 30 483; call 30 484
narrate Breaker panel: DOORS. A bang, a shower of sparks, and every breaker in the wing snaps back open.
narrate Taped to the panel: COLD START. CORE, LIGHTS, DOORS. IN THAT ORDER.
say android17 Read the instructions, Eighteen.
say android18 You pulled it, not me.
stop
label brkd_on
narrate All three breakers are closed. The power is on.
list wing_lower_locked
narrate The lower corridor is shuttered and dark. A sign over it reads BIO WING. NO POWER: RESTORE AT THE BREAKERS.
say android17 The breaker panels. Of course it couldn't just be a switch.
do call 120 10; call 119 1 111 1 220 370; call 121 10
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch7_bio
set_flag 481
narrate The bio wing. Two great machines hang from the ceiling, their red eyes dark. A catwalk crosses a tank of green fluid.
narrate On the catwalk, something big unfolds itself and turns toward the door.
narrate Computer: Unregistered units in the bio wing. Warden, protect the samples.
journal Destroy the bio wing's {c07}warden{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list bio_units_door
narrate A sealed door. UNITS 13 / 14 / 15. TRANSFERRED: NORTHERN BUNKER, CONSTRUCTION BAY.
say android17 So that's where the computer keeps its toys.
list bio_monitor
unless_flag 482 monitor_guarded
if_flag 486 monitor_again
set_flag 486
narrate A monitor on its own circuit, still running. INCUBATOR LINK: NORTHERN BUNKER, LOWER LEVEL.
do call 120 30; call 115 17 25 1 140 150; call 121 30
narrate A pod in the dark. Something small is curled up inside it, green and spotted. It twitches.
narrate Computer: Project Cell. Growth nominal. Estimated maturity: twenty-one years.
do call 120 30; call 119 1 116 1 448 184; call 121 30
say android18 What was that thing?
say android17 Something that won't be ready for twenty-one years. Let it be somebody else's problem.
say android18 And when it is ready?
say android17 Then we'll be bored, and it'll be something to do.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label monitor_again
narrate INCUBATOR LINK. The pod. The twitching shape. Twenty-one years.
stop
label monitor_guarded
narrate A monitor across the catwalk. The warden is between it and the twins.
# ---------- Gero's notes 4 and 5 (flags 523 / 524)
list note_wing
if_flag 523 nwing_read
set_flag 523
narrate A notebook page under the console's keyboard.
narrate "Units 17 and 18 refuse every order. I could correct it in an hour. I don't. I tell myself it is scientific curiosity."
say android18 Him again.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label nwing_read
narrate The console. Nothing else under the keyboard.
list note_archive
if_flag 524 narch_read
set_flag 524
narrate One notebook on the shelf has a page torn half out, as if someone started to throw it away and stopped.
narrate "The shutdown controller works. I keep it in my coat. I have had a hundred reasons to use it. I wonder if I ever will."
say android17 He didn't. Too slow.
say android18 Or he didn't want to.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label narch_read
narrate Gero's notebooks. Thousands of pages. Nobody will ever read them all.
# ---------- Gero's Quarters (second length pass, log4/gen_more.py ch7_quarters; 534 arrival, 538 diary, 535 key,
# 536 safe opened (the sentry wakes), 537 sentry destroyed, 539 safe emptied)
list ch7_quarters
set_flag 534
narrate A bedroom. A real one: a bed, a lamp, a picture on the wall. Ten steps of rock away from the pods.
say android18 He slept here? Next door to us?
say android17 Even mad scientists need a bed. Let's see what the old man kept for himself.
list quarters_diary
set_flag 538
narrate A diary on the nightstand, the last pages written in a shaking hand.
narrate "Gevo would have laughed at me. Twenty years of work, and the two finest machines I ever built won't take a single order."
narrate "I keep the key where Gevo would look first. He always went straight for my desk photograph, to straighten it. He hated a crooked frame."
narrate "I keep the switch on me. The spare, and its blueprints, stay in the safe. They must never fall into their hands."
say android18 A spare off switch. In case the first one got broken.
say android17 Like that one did. Let's break this one too.
list quarters_photo
if_flag 535 photo_after
set_flag 535
narrate A framed photograph on the dresser: a young man in a Red Ribbon uniform, grinning at the camera. The frame sits crooked.
say android18 Gevo. His son. The one in the diary.
narrate Seventeen straightens the frame. A small brass key drops out from behind it.
say android17 The key's where his son would look first. Sentimental old man.
stop
label photo_after
narrate Gevo's photograph. The frame is straight now.
list quarters_bed
narrate The bed is made with military corners. The pillow has never been slept on.
say android18 He never even used it.
list quarters_safe
if_flag 539 safe_empty
if_flag 536 safe_open
unless_flag 535 safe_locked
set_flag 536
narrate Behind the painting, a steel safe. The brass key turns.
narrate Computer: Unauthorised access. Private quarters. Sentry activated.
do call 120 30; call 119 1 117 1 256 72; call 121 30
stop
label safe_open
unless_flag 537 safe_guarded
set_flag 539
narrate Inside the safe: a second black handset with two buttons, marked 17 and 18. A folder of blueprints underneath. And a medical kit.
say android18 One press, and we're switched off. That's all we were to him.
narrate Seventeen crushes the remote in one hand and lets the pieces drop. Eighteen feeds the blueprints into the lamp, page by page.
say android17 Nobody's switching us off. Not him, not anyone.
do call 129 11 2; call 129 8 1; call 129 10 1
narrate Got 2 Senzu Beans, a Super Elixir and a Holy Water.
stop
label safe_guarded
narrate The sentry stands between you and the safe.
stop
label safe_locked
narrate Behind the painting, a steel safe with a small brass keyhole. It's locked.
unless_flag 538 safe_nohint
say android18 Read the diary, Seventeen. He kept the key where his son would look first.
stop
label safe_nohint
say android17 Locked. The old man kept his key somewhere in here.
stop
label safe_empty
narrate The safe stands empty. Bits of the remote are still on the floor.
